---
source: crates/standalone/fixture/src/lib.rs
---
Download the site, or the files the last push sent, to a
folder.

Usage: ink export [OPTIONS] [DIR]

Examples
  ink export out           # The live site's files, into out
  ink export --source src  # The files the last push sent

Arguments
  [DIR]  The folder to write: new, or empty
         [default: export]

Options
      --source
        Download the files the last push sent, not the site
        they built
      --deploy <DEPLOY>
        Download this deploy, by the start of its id, not
        the live one
      --max-files <N>
        Most files the archive may hold [default: 100000]
      --max-file <BYTES>
        Most bytes one file may hold [default: 104857600]
      --max-bytes <BYTES>
        Most bytes all the files may hold
        [default: 2147483648]
      --max-name <BYTES>
        Longest file name, in bytes [default: 1024]

Account
      --api <URL>
        The API's address, `http://host[:port]`;
        `account.api` in the config file [env: INK_API]
      --site <ID>
        The site's id; `account.site` in the config file
        [env: INK_SITE]
      --org <ID>
        Act as this organization, by its id: the site is one
        of its sites, and the key's role there is what is
        checked. See `ink org list` [env: INK_ORG]
      --timeout <SECONDS>
        Seconds one call may take [default: 30]
        [env: INK_TIMEOUT]
      --retries <N>
        How many more times a call that is safe to repeat is
        tried when the network fails [default: 2]
        [env: INK_RETRIES]
      --retry-wait <MS>
        Milliseconds before the first retry; each wait is
        twice the one before [default: 500]
        [env: INK_RETRY_WAIT]

Notes
  Writes into a new or empty folder, through a staging
  folder beside it, so a failure leaves no partial folder.
  The live site's files are named by route, with `index` for
  the root.

Exit codes
  0  Done
  2  Wrong usage: no site named, an id that is none, a
     deploy the site lacks
  3  Not signed in, or the token was refused
  4  The API could not be reached or failed; safe to retry
  5  The API refused the change as it stands: the deploy is
     already live, say

Environment
  INK_API       The address of the API, as --api
  INK_SITE      The site's id, as --site
  INK_KEY       The private key to sign requests with, for a
                CI job; never a flag, so it stays out of
                process lists. `ink login` keeps one in the
                config folder instead
  INK_KEY_FILE  A file that holds that key, in place of
                INK_KEY

See also  ink push, ink build
Docs      https://github.com/uses-ink/uses.ink/blob/main/docs/cli.md
Global    -C, --json, -q, -v, --color, --no-progress, --log,
          --log-file (see `ink --help`)
